This branch generates a hybrid mesh for an eccentric annular domain.

The mesh has three regions:

    structured quadrilateral boundary layer at the inner cylinder
    recombined unstructured Gmsh quadrilateral core
    structured quadrilateral boundary layer at the outer cylinder

Geometry, independent inner/outer circumferential divisions, boundary-layer
thicknesses and coreMeshSize are configured in params.h. Boundary topology and
derived radial layer counts are defined in edgefunctions.h. mesh.cpp implements
the two-stage generation and merge flow.

Run:

    ./make.sh

This writes core.geo, meshes it with Gmsh 2.14 in MSH2 format, merges the core
with both boundary layers, and writes ring.xml. A different output name can be
given as the first argument:

    ./make.sh my-ring.xml

Boundary composites in the final Nektar++ XML are:

    C[0]  inner cylinder wall
    C[1]  outer cylinder wall
